# Package list for the minimal Raspberry Pi 5 bootc image.
#
# Lines beginning with '#' and blank lines are ignored. Everything else the
# system needs (systemd, dnf, bootc, podman-free basics, coreutils, vim-minimal,
# openssh-clients, ...) already comes from the fedora-bootc base — only add what
# the base does NOT ship. Keep this list SHORT; this is an appliance, not a
# workstation.

# --- Raspberry Pi 5 boot chain (BUILD-TIME ONLY) -------------------------
# The Pi 5 EEPROM has no UEFI: it loads the GPU firmware + DTB from a FAT32
# partition, then U-Boot, which provides the EFI environment GRUB/bootc needs.
# scripts/configure.sh relocates these files to /usr/lib/bootc-rpi-firmware and
# REMOVES both packages again (they install into /boot/efi, which a bootc image
# must not own); a bootupctl shim copies them onto the ESP at install time.
bcm283x-firmware
bcm283x-overlays
uboot-images-armv8

# --- Hardware ------------------------------------------------------------
# Pi 5 Wi-Fi/BT is a CYW43455 (brcmfmac). linux-firmware no longer bundles the
# per-vendor blobs, so request the Broadcom split explicitly.
brcmfmac-firmware
# Some drivers ship only in the "extra" kernel-modules split, not the base
# kernel package the bootc base pulls in.
kernel-modules-extra

# --- Grow the rootfs to fill the card on first boot ----------------------
# bootc-generic-growpart.service needs /usr/bin/growpart (ConditionPathExists),
# and the base image does not ship it. Without this the root filesystem stays at
# the image's ~8.5 GiB and the rest of the card is wasted. See the drop-in in
# overlay/ that also lifts the unit's ConditionVirtualization=vm guard.
cloud-utils-growpart

# --- Networking ----------------------------------------------------------
NetworkManager
NetworkManager-wifi
iproute
iputils
# REQUIRED, not a nicety: the Pi 5 has NO RTC, so it boots with the image's build
# date and every TLS handshake fails ("certificate is not yet valid") until
# something corrects the clock. That breaks the first `podman pull` of every
# Quadlet image on the box. configure.sh enables chronyd.
chrony

# --- Remote access (this is a HEADLESS device) ---------------------------
openssh-server

# --- Containers (the point of an image-mode host) ------------------------
podman
crun
# Explicit because weak deps are off: podman pulls this as a Recommends on some
# builds, and without it every container bind-mount trips SELinux on enforcing.
container-selinux

# --- Day-2 -------------------------------------------------------------
# bootc + podman are what ./fedora-update needs on the device itself.
bootc
sudo
